    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48511" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεσμοθέτ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίθημι</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lawgiver, legislator</i>,
			of <i><span class="en">
				Moses
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				9.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> esp. at
			Athens, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεσμοθέται, οἱ</span>, the <i>six junior archons,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12.39.75
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				775
			</span></i> (sg.), al., <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				6.35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				3.4
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.38
			</span></i>; also, title of magistrate in Amorgos, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(7).57.12
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>.</div>
